  "notes": "Historical build for the 2024-25 catalog edition. Source: https://bulletins.psu.edu/archive/2024-2025/undergraduate/colleges/liberal-arts/spanish-ba/ (raw HTML fetched; Suggested Academic Plan subtotals sum to 120, matching the page's own printed 'Total Credits 120' and matching the Program Requirements table's own Requirement/Credits breakdown [45 + 15 + 24 + 36 = 120]). Real, confirmed differences from 2023-24: (1) The Fall-of-fourth-year Elective present in 2022-23 and 2023-24 is gone this edition -- that semester drops from 16.5cr to 13.5cr (ENGL 202B + GEN ED (GHW) + one 200-/300-level SPAN + one 400-level Literature + one 400-level Linguistics, no trailing Elective), which is exactly the same 13.5cr Semester-7 shape the live 2026 file already uses -- confirmed by diffing the fetched SAP tables directly. (2) SPAN 200's alternate is unambiguously SPAN 200A this edition (SPAN 301 no longer appears anywhere on the page, in either the Program Requirements or Suggested Academic Plan tab) -- the Spring-2024 transition documented in the 2023 file's own notes is fully resolved by this edition. (3) The B.A. degree-requirement label switches from 'B.A. Other Cultures' to 'B.A. World Cultures' this edition (confirmed in both the Suggested Academic Plan text and the Program Requirements ' B.A. Degree Requirements' section, which itself relabels 'Other Cultures' to 'World Cultures' and 'Foreign Language'/'Foreign Study' to 'World Language'/'Foreign Study' -- a university-wide terminology change, not SPANBA-specific). LA 83 / LA 283 seminars: still absent from this edition's Suggested Academic Plan (confirmed absent in all of 2022-23 through 2024-25; first appear in 2025-26). 200-/300-level supporting list, 400-level Hispanic Linguistics, 400-level Hispanic Literature, and the 400-level general list are identical to the 2023-24 edition (same SPAN 300B/315N/411/417/470/474/491 additions carried forward) -- confirmed by diffing the fetched PR tables. Bare 'SPAN 210' and 'SPAN 354' again appear on this edition's PR page (SPAN 210's title cell is blank on this fetch, unlike prior years -- consistent with the course nearing retirement in favor of SPAN 210N) but are omitted here, same convention as every other year in this batch. Campus: confirmed 'End Campus: University Park' only on this archived page too. No real reason found to suspect course-level prerequisites differed from the live catalog, so the department course-description archive was not separately re-fetched.",
